
=== features block ===

-- COP learner duty floor keys on the modulation floor (live v6.7.17)
  ok   a 14 kW nameplate pump drawing 1.9-2.55 kW teaches the COP learner once the meter shows the draw follows the ask
  ok   while draw evidence is pending a departure is held on any nameplate, and reads as awaiting it; with no window base's rule stands (14 kW refuses, 4 kW folds) and nothing is held
  ok   idle and standby draws under the modulation floor still teach nothing
  ok   with no modulation floor configured the nameplate floor still applies
  ok   the duty floor is 0.8 x the modulation floor, never below 0.2 kW
  ok   the flow-lift fold takes the same floor: a 14 kW nameplate at 2.2 kW folds
  ok   a hot-water-dominant window under a space plan folds no flow-bias sample; an all-space window folds one (null)
  ok   the flow-lift gate's no-weight bound is inclusive: a 1e-6 h window folds nothing, a 2e-6 h window folds one (null)
  ok   a hot-water share exactly at the curve share still folds; just above it does not (null)
  ok   a switch-back interval gives the house learners no space power; an all-space dwell books the reading and an unobserved one the plan's subtraction, as before (nulls)
  ok   without a power entity a switch-back interval books no commanded space power; an all-space dwell books the ask (null)
  ok   a hot-water dwell under a space plan folds no running-draw sample; an all-space dwell and an unobserved interval fold one each (nulls)
  ok   a refused COP interval names its guard and the floor in the diagnostics
  ok   a folded COP interval clears the refusal
  ok   each guard has its own code: a freeze and a missing reading
  ok   a draw that ignores a varying ask is refused as off-ask, and under a flat ask it folds nothing while the heat-ask probe is pending (the scale at 1.000 or one of its two dither levels, 0.9325 and 1.0724); a matched draw and a 0.7 shift on a draw that follows its ask still teach
  ok   follows_ask: no evidence without the window, before MIN_SAMPLES, or on a flat ask; a proportional draw follows, a self-set one does not
  ok   the last measured COP and its curve are restored on restart
  ok   an unreadable stored COP record loads as no measurement, whole
  ok   an unreadable stored COP record loads as no measurement, whole
  ok   an unreadable stored COP record loads as no measurement, whole
  ok   an unreadable stored COP record loads as no measurement, whole
  ok   an unreadable stored COP record loads as no measurement, whole
  ok   an unreadable stored COP record loads as no measurement, whole
  ok   the duty floor judges the smaller of the ask and the draw: a plan asked 2.4 kW that metered 0.3 kW is refused, and so the other way round
  ok   the duty floor is exclusive: a draw exactly at it is running, not below it
  ok   the tracking gate divides by the clamped walking ratio: a zero ewma is a refusal, not a crash
  ok   the tracking gate is exclusive: a ratio exactly at it is on the walking ratio (6.5 against 5.0 is 0.3 of it)
  ok   without draw evidence the nameplate bar is on both the ask and the drawn figure: a 5.0 kW ask metering 4.0 kW waits for evidence, one metering 4.5 kW folds (0.3 x 14 is 4.2 exactly)
  ok   the store's 0.1 bar is exclusive and a non-finite tank temperature drops the record whole: 0.1 reads back, a nan temperature does not
  ok   follows_ask gives evidence at 48 running samples and none at 47, and it answers a bool, never None, once it has them
  ok   asks spanning exactly 1.15 are evidence (the span bound is `<`), and an ask exactly at the configured floor counts as a running level
  ok   a draw whose log-log slope is exactly 0.5, and whose level moves by exactly 1.25 across the span, follows the ask (both bounds inclusive)
  ok   a sample asked nothing is not a running level: with no configured minimum the positive-ask half of the filter still drops it

-- R10-COP-LEARNER-DRAW-FLOOR: the floor capped by the run-asked draw, and hold-then-replay
  ok   a pump metered running at 0.6 x its ask on an overstated 3.0 kW minimum has its floor capped at that draw's low end, 1.8 kW (configured 2.4)
  ok   (a) the cap never raises the floor: draws equal to, or 1.5 x, the ask leave the configured 2.4 kW, bit for bit
  ok   (b) the floor never goes under on_threshold_kw: a low end of 0.9 kW reads 1.5 kW, half the 3.0 kW minimum
  ok   (c) no window, an empty one, and one of 47 run-asked pairs leave the configured floor bit for bit; the 48th caps it
  ok   (d) a draw under an ask below the configured minimum never moves the floor: alone it leaves 2.4 kW, beside 48 run-asked draws of 2.0 kW the floor is 2.0, and an ask exactly at the minimum is a run ask
  ok   (e) a window keyed to another configured range caps nothing: a changed minimum or maximum reads its own configured floor at once, and the next sample drops the old window
  ok   (f) with no modulation floor configured the nameplate third stands uncapped, whatever the window metered (60 pairs drawing 0.5 kW)
  ok   judge_floor reads the capped floor on the window it is handed: 2.0 kW is refused without the window and folds with it, 1.7 kW is under the cap
  ok   a 2.0 kW interval on a 3.0 kW minimum folds its COP and its flow lift once the window has metered the pump running at 1.8 kW, and the diagnostics name that floor; with an empty window all three read 2.4 kW
  ok   the flow-lift fold takes an ask exactly at the floor and refuses one a nanowatt under it, on the window's cap (1.8 kW) and on the configured figure (2.4 kW)
  ok   with no power reading the running-draw window stays empty, so the span close's floor is the configured one
  ok   ask_evidence: follows and does-not-follow on 48 run-asked pairs whose asks span; pending on an empty window and on 47 pairs
  ok   ask_evidence is unobtainable with no window, on asks that never moved, and on a full window (336) holding 0 or 34 run-asked pairs; one sample short of full it is still pending
  ok   follows_ask is that state as a tri-state: None for both waiting states
  FAIL the measured shape (slope 0.70, drawn 2.1 x the ask at the low end of the span and 1.4 x at the top) does not follow its ask; one 1.70 x shift and a draw within tolerance of its ask follow, a self-set draw still does not  [('follows', 'follows', 'follows', 'does_not_follow')]
  FAIL a flat draw over asks spanning 1.2 fails on the slope, a square-law draw over asks spanning 1.5 fails on the level  [('does_not_follow', 'follows')]
  FAIL a departure is held, and reads as awaiting evidence, only while the evidence is pending: it folds on follows, is off-ask on does-not-follow, and takes base's rule with nothing held where there is no window; where the window's evidence is unobtainable the heat-ask probe takes it, and while that is pending the interval is held, as any other awaiting evidence  [('awaiting_draw_evidence', 1) / (None, 0) / (None, 0) / (None, 0) / ('awaiting_draw_evidence', 0)]
  ok   once the meter shows the draw follows the ask, a departure under the nameplate third teaches: 2.0 kW drawing 2.6 on 14 kW folds and is not held, where the same interval with no window is refused for want of evidence (control)
  ok   an interval inside the ask tolerance, or one the tracking gate refuses, is never held
  ok   an interval's ratio divides by the ask clamped at 1e-6: a zero ask is a huge ratio for the tracking gate to refuse, not a ZeroDivisionError
  ok   walk_ratio hands back the value before the interval (1.0 the first time) and walks a tenth of the way
  ok   release: evidence empties the hold -- every row, oldest first, where the draw follows the ask; none where it does not
  FAIL release: with no window the hold empties by base's rule -- the row clearing the nameplate third folds, the other is dropped; where the window's evidence is unobtainable and the heat-ask probe is pending, both rows wait and nothing folds  [([(5.0, 6.0)], 0) / ([(5.0, 6.0)], 0)]
  ok   release: while the evidence is pending a row waits a week and no longer -- at 7 days exactly both wait, a second later both leave by base's rule
  FAIL release: no fold lands on a pending heat-ask probe however long it lasts -- under unobtainable evidence both rows wait at 7 days exactly, and a second later both are dropped, the one base's rule folds included  [([(5.0, 6.0)], 0) / ([(5.0, 6.0)], 0)]
  ok   release: a row stamped ahead of the clock has no knowable age and does not wait on it -- it leaves by base's rule; one a second old waits
  ok   release: a row stamped at the clock itself is zero seconds old and waits; a microsecond ahead of the clock it leaves by base's rule
  ok   release: with a window that does not grow, each row leaves on its own week -- at day 8 the older folds and the 3-day-younger waits
  ok   base's rule folds a departure whose ask sits exactly on the nameplate third and refuses one just under it
  ok   release: the hold is bounded at 336 rows; the row pushed out is judged by base's rule, not lost and not folded unjudged (336 rows push none out)
  ok   a released interval folds against the scale it was read at, and the interval that released it keeps its own refusal
  ok   a released interval is judged against the curve of the cycle it was read on: one read on a space cycle folds when a blended cycle releases it, and one read on a blended cycle trains nothing when a space cycle releases it
  ok   a frozen cycle and one with no power reading release nothing and fold nothing; the next live cycle releases the held interval
  ok   a replayed interval folds the scale and not the capacity envelope; the same evidence folded live feeds the envelope (control)
  ok   the diagnostics publish the floor to the watt: a 1.2345 kW minimum's 0.9876 kW floor reads 0.988
  ok   the diagnostics count the held intervals beside the evidence they wait on
  ok   a pump that sets its own power folds no departure while the evidence is pending: on 4 kW the scale stays within 0.02 of 1.0 (base: 0.789) and the hold is empty once the evidence has dropped it
  ok   a pump whose draw follows its ask loses no held interval: more than 280 of 288 fold (base: 241), none twice, and the scale reaches 0.7
  FAIL (h) with a window that never reaches evidence the heat ask is probed, nothing folds while that is pending, and no interval is lost once it reads follows: a heat-led pump of true 0.8 folds 96 of 96 behind a full window; behind one that fills at the 48th it is still pending at the 96th, all 96 held, inside the dither band, and over 192 it folds 192; 40 intervals into the filling one, all 40 are still held; the fixed 3.2 kW draw folds nothing and ends does_not_follow at the configured scale  [heat-led full (96, 0.8107, 'follows', 0); filling (96, 0.8099, 'follows', 0); filling x192 (192, 0.8005, 'follows', 0); part 0 folded, 40 held; fixed 3.2 kW [(47, 1.0, 'does_not_follow', 0), (53, 1.0, 'does_not_follow', 0), (53, 1.0, 'does_not_follow', 0)]]
  ok   a release that steps the fold count over a multiple of ten saves the learning (7 + 5 -> 12); one landing on it saves (9 + 1); one that crosses none does not (10 + 3, 3 + 0)

